From: Marionette <marionette@localhost>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] deliver AWDL data frames to the host-only sink

marionette_monitor_post_frame() starts with

	if (frame[0] != 0xd0)
		return;

0xd0 is a management Action frame, so every non-action frame is dropped at the
door.  That was invisible while the only consumer was a counter, but it is fatal
for the sink: the frames that carry AirDrop's mDNS service advertisements -- and,
later, the file payload itself -- are 802.11 QoS *data* frames, not action
frames.  Measured on device 2026-10-23 with patch 0047 delivering action frames
correctly:

	mon_desc_data        144821   (data frames do reach the monitor ring)
	mon_post_awdl           452   (only action frames were classified)
	mdns_rx_other             0   (filin never saw a peer's mDNS)

so the ring was carrying data all along and this check was throwing it away.

AWDL data frames are identified the same way the action ones are: the AWDL BSSID
in addr3 (00:25:00:ff:94:73).  They do not carry the 7f 00 17 f2 08 10 action
prefix, which is exactly why the existing predicate cannot be reused.

This is the smallest change that admits them: relax the type check, add a data
predicate keyed on addr3, and count deliveries separately so the two populations
stay distinguishable.  No firmware interaction, no new vdev, no channel change.

Not addressed here: the sink's radiotap header still carries no TSFT field, so
filin cannot compute tsf_offset_us and reports synced=false.  That needs the
descriptor timestamp plumbed into marionette_monitor_post_frame(), which is a
separate change.

--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_rx_mon_dest_1.0.c
@@ -135,6 +135,10 @@ module_param_cb(marionette_awdl_sink_rx, &marionette_mon_counter_ops,
 module_param_cb(marionette_awdl_sink_drop, &marionette_mon_counter_ops,
 		&marionette_awdl_sink_drop, 0400);
 
+static atomic_long_t marionette_mon_post_data = ATOMIC_LONG_INIT(0);
+module_param_cb(marionette_mon_post_data, &marionette_mon_counter_ops,
+		&marionette_mon_post_data, 0400);
+
 static struct net_device *marionette_sink_dev;
 static void marionette_sink_create(struct work_struct *work);
 static DECLARE_WORK(marionette_sink_work, marionette_sink_create);
@@ -337,8 +341,24 @@ void marionette_monitor_post_frame(const u8 *frame, u32 length)
 	    !frame || length < 2)
 		return;
 	atomic_long_inc(&marionette_mon_post_total);
-	if (frame[0] != 0xd0)
+	if (frame[0] != 0xd0) {
+		static const u8 awdl_bssid[] = {0, 0x25, 0, 0xff, 0x94, 0x73};
+
+		/*
+		 * AWDL data frames -- the ones carrying mDNS and, later, the
+		 * AirDrop payload -- are QoS data with the AWDL BSSID in addr3.
+		 * They never carry the action prefix, so the predicate below
+		 * cannot classify them; without this branch the sink only ever
+		 * sees PSF/MIF and filin reports mdns_rx_other = 0.
+		 */
+		if ((frame[0] & 0x0c) != 0x08 || length < 24 ||
+		    memcmp(frame + 16, awdl_bssid, sizeof(awdl_bssid)))
+			return;
+		atomic_long_inc(&marionette_mon_post_data);
+		if (marionette_awdl_sink)
+			marionette_awdl_sink_deliver(frame, length);
 		return;
+	}
 	atomic_long_inc(&marionette_mon_post_action);
 	if (!marionette_monitor_is_awdl(frame, length))
 		return;
